So, as a developer, I
don't have direct access

00:40:43.880 --> 00:40:45.270
to cloud console anymore.

00:40:45.270 --> 00:40:47.720
I cannot go to console
and create my project here

00:40:47.720 --> 00:40:50.780
and manually specify
the IAM policies there.

00:40:50.780 --> 00:40:54.740
Instead, I'll be doing all
of that through the repo

00:40:54.740 --> 00:40:57.500
by going through the
code review process.

00:40:57.500 --> 00:41:00.990
With that, I'm going
to my cloud shell.

00:41:00.990 --> 00:41:02.615
And I'm also going
to run the script.

00:41:06.510 --> 00:41:08.760
So as a developer, the
first thing I need to do

00:41:08.760 --> 00:41:10.950
is I'm going to clone
my company's repository

00:41:10.950 --> 00:41:12.834
into my local environment.

00:41:18.050 --> 00:41:20.120
As we can see, all
the data is here.

00:41:20.120 --> 00:41:21.785
So open the cloud shell editor.

00:41:24.580 --> 00:41:27.100
Now the repo is here
containing everything

00:41:27.100 --> 00:41:28.765
that me and Alice just pushed.

00:41:32.950 --> 00:41:36.580
So I'm going to create this
project under the folder

00:41:36.580 --> 00:41:37.840
Engineering.

00:41:37.840 --> 00:41:39.560
How am I going to do that?

00:41:39.560 --> 00:41:41.900
So just like the two other
existing projects, Checkout

00:41:41.900 --> 00:41:43.780
Service and Shopping
Cart Service,

00:41:43.780 --> 00:41:47.900
I'm going to do that by creating
a new directory for my project.

00:41:47.900 --> 00:41:51.050
So I'm going to navigate
to this directory.

00:41:51.050 --> 00:41:53.740
And in this demo, I'm going
to just copy over the files

00:41:53.740 --> 00:41:56.470
that I prepared beforehand.

00:41:56.470 --> 00:41:59.940
So now, you see I have created
a new directory under the folder

00:41:59.940 --> 00:42:00.580
Engineering.

00:42:00.580 --> 00:42:03.400
It's called Project Fulfillment.

00:42:03.400 --> 00:42:07.060
And I have created a
gcp-project.yaml which contains

00:42:07.060 --> 00:42:09.260
the [INAUDIBLE]
of my new project.

00:42:09.260 --> 00:42:12.960
I named my project
Fulfillment Service.

00:42:12.960 --> 00:42:18.120
And in the gcp-iampolicy.yaml,
I specified Bob from gmail.com

00:42:18.120 --> 00:42:20.700
as a project editor.

00:42:20.700 --> 00:42:23.175
Now as a developer, I'm going
to create a pull request.

00:42:37.280 --> 00:42:40.220
So now, the pull
request gets created.

00:42:40.220 --> 00:42:42.760
And you see that Cloud
Build runs immediately.

00:42:42.760 --> 00:42:44.980
So Cloud Build, in
this case, performed

00:42:44.980 --> 00:42:46.400
as our [INAUDIBLE] check.

00:42:46.400 --> 00:42:48.800
It runs our config
validator, which

00:42:48.800 --> 00:42:52.090
does a bunch of [INAUDIBLE]
checks against or repo.

00:42:52.090 --> 00:42:56.110
For example, it checks for
project ID duplication.

00:42:56.110 --> 00:42:59.150
It cannot have two projects
having the same ID.

00:42:59.150 --> 00:43:02.510
It also checks for GCP
hierarchy violations.

00:43:02.510 --> 00:43:06.040
For example, you cannot have to
create a GCP product and then

00:43:06.040 --> 00:43:08.002
another GCP product.

00:43:08.002 --> 00:43:09.460
In addition to
that, it also checks

00:43:09.460 --> 00:43:12.610
for IAM policy violations
against the rules, the policy

00:43:12.610 --> 00:43:14.908
constraints that we
put into this repo.

00:43:14.908 --> 00:43:17.200
Actually in this case, we
see that Cloud Build actually

00:43:17.200 --> 00:43:18.370
has failed.

00:43:18.370 --> 00:43:21.470
So let's go to Cloud Build page.

00:43:21.470 --> 00:43:24.230
So this is the one we just run.

00:43:24.230 --> 00:43:26.480
Open it.

00:43:26.480 --> 00:43:28.380
So from the log,
we see that it's

00:43:28.380 --> 00:43:32.530
reporting two errors, one from
duplicate project ID, Shopping

00:43:32.530 --> 00:43:33.880
Cart Service.

00:43:33.880 --> 00:43:36.150
So if we circle back,
this is basically

00:43:36.150 --> 00:43:39.850
complaining that I'm using
a duplicated project ID.

00:43:39.850 --> 00:43:44.430
So this ID already
exists today on GCP.

00:43:44.430 --> 00:43:50.110
And second error complains,
found a constraint violation.

00:43:50.110 --> 00:43:53.710
So contains member
from unexpected domain,

00:43:53.710 --> 00:43:56.680
devbob@gmail.com So
this is basically

00:43:56.680 --> 00:44:00.190
because Bob has specified
his personal gmail account

00:44:00.190 --> 00:44:04.300
as a project editor, which
clearly violates the policy

00:44:04.300 --> 00:44:07.300
constraints or violates
the company's compliance.

00:44:07.300 --> 00:44:09.850
So with these two
errors, as a developer

00:44:09.850 --> 00:44:11.710
I've realized that
I should really

00:44:11.710 --> 00:44:14.530
be running the config
validator locally before I even

00:44:14.530 --> 00:44:16.420
create this pull request.

00:44:16.420 --> 00:44:17.920
So I go back to my repo.

00:44:17.920 --> 00:44:19.930
I'm going to run the
config validator through.

00:44:27.898 --> 00:44:29.400
It takes a while.

00:44:29.400 --> 00:44:32.870
So indeed, it's reporting
these two violations--

00:44:32.870 --> 00:44:35.600
the domain violation and
the project ID violation.

00:44:35.600 --> 00:44:37.520
So let's fix these two errors.

00:44:37.520 --> 00:44:41.240
First, let's not use gmail,
which violates the rule.

00:44:41.240 --> 00:44:42.965
Let's use Chili Oregano.

00:44:47.920 --> 00:44:50.380
And let's give the new
project a unique ID.

00:44:59.120 --> 00:45:03.370
Now let's run the config
validator through again.

00:45:03.370 --> 00:45:06.840
See this time there's no errors.

00:45:06.840 --> 00:45:08.730
So I'm going to update
the pull request.

00:45:14.970 --> 00:45:17.040
Now Cloud Build runs again.

00:45:21.580 --> 00:45:22.430
Let's open the logs.

00:45:25.420 --> 00:45:28.670
So while Cloud Build is running,
let's do another quick recap.

00:45:28.670 --> 00:45:34.120
So as a developer, I propose
config changes through the repo

00:45:34.120 --> 00:45:36.040
by creating new pull request.

00:45:36.040 --> 00:45:38.920
And the config validator
will capture and report

00:45:38.920 --> 00:45:42.310
any errors that are introduced
by my config changes.

00:45:42.310 --> 00:45:45.940
I will be able to fix these
errors before the bad changes

00:45:45.940 --> 00:45:48.160
get pushed on the [INAUDIBLE].

00:45:48.160 --> 00:45:50.800
So now in this case, we see
that Cloud Build is happy.

00:45:54.210 --> 00:45:58.850
So now, imagine I'm Alice,
the cloud administrator again.

00:45:58.850 --> 00:46:02.960
So I receive a notification
of a new pull request.

00:46:02.960 --> 00:46:10.840
So I go to my GitHub account,
open this pull request.

00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:12.340
Actually, I notice
that all checks

00:46:12.340 --> 00:46:15.370
are passed for these pull
requests, which is great.

00:46:15.370 --> 00:46:18.110
I go inspect the code changes.

00:46:18.110 --> 00:46:21.650
I see that Bob is going to
create a fulfillment service

00:46:21.650 --> 00:46:22.430
project.

00:46:22.430 --> 00:46:25.460
And Bob has specified
his corporate account

00:46:25.460 --> 00:46:27.730
as the project editor.

00:46:27.730 --> 00:46:30.278
So the code looks fine to me.

00:46:30.278 --> 00:46:32.195
I'm going to merge this
pull request directly.

00:46:36.210 --> 00:46:38.360
So now the pull
request gets merged.

00:46:38.360 --> 00:46:40.070
So what happens next?

00:46:40.070 --> 00:46:43.690
So this repo is already being
enabled with Anthos Config

00:46:43.690 --> 00:46:44.690
Management.

00:46:44.690 --> 00:46:46.370
And the master
branch is currently

00:46:46.370 --> 00:46:48.870
being actively monitored
by the service.

00:46:48.870 --> 00:46:51.080
So if it detects
any new changes,

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:53.450
it will automatically
pick them up and apply

00:46:53.450 --> 00:46:55.610
to the underlying GCP platform.

00:46:55.610 --> 00:46:58.400
That means the new project
Fulfillment Service

00:46:58.400 --> 00:47:01.310
project will get created
automatically on GCP.

00:47:01.310 --> 00:47:04.410
And Bob will be specified
as the project editor.

00:47:04.410 --> 00:47:07.687
So now let's go to the
console and verify.

00:47:07.687 --> 00:47:08.270
Let's refresh.

00:47:13.960 --> 00:47:17.680
So now we see that fulfillment
service project appears right

00:47:17.680 --> 00:47:20.590
under the Engineering folder.

00:47:20.590 --> 00:47:25.910
If we look at IAM policies,
now bob@chilioregano.com

00:47:25.910 --> 00:47:28.920
is now specified as
a project editor.

00:47:28.920 --> 00:47:31.230
So, yeah, that's pretty much
the demo I have for today.

00:47:31.230 --> 00:47:33.230
With that, I'm going
to hand over to Marco.

